From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 12:30:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] vkd3d: Handle raw buffers in optimized ClearUAV path

Raw buffer UAV descriptors use DXGI_FORMAT_UNKNOWN.  The legacy clear path
already interprets those descriptors as R32_UINT, but the optimized clear path
added by 7f410b766e2f dereferences the result of looking up the unknown format.
This causes a NULL dereference in d3d12_command_list_clear_uav_builtin(), seen
while The Witcher 3 initializes its DX12 renderer.

Use the same R32_UINT format selected for raw buffers by the fallback path and
reject any other unrecognized format before accessing it.

Fixes: https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/issues/720
---
 libs/vkd3d/command.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libs/vkd3d/command.c b/libs/vkd3d/command.c
index 5e82fcc4..d69a4d5b 100644
--- a/libs/vkd3d/command.c
+++ b/libs/vkd3d/command.c
@@ -16050,6 +16050,18 @@
             uint_format = vkd3d_get_format(list->device, DXGI_FORMAT_R32_UINT, false);
         }
 
+       /* Raw buffer UAVs use DXGI_FORMAT_UNKNOWN (0), so clear_format is NULL.
+        * Set it to the same R32_UINT format used above, matching the fallback path. */
+       if (!clear_format)
+           clear_format = uint_format;
+
+       /* Reject any other unrecognized format before dereferencing. */
+       if (!clear_format)
+       {
+           ERR("Invalid format for buffer UAV clear.\n");
+           return;
+       }
+
         args.clear_dxgi_format = uint_format->dxgi_format;
 
         args.heap_index = d3d12_command_list_allocate_meta_buffer_view(list,
